<a name="firebirdwirecrypt"/><h1>Wire Encryption</h1>

<p>Firebird 3 and later encrypt the traffic between client and server with their own wire encryption, rather than with TLS/SSL, and the Firebird protocol module does the same.  The encryption is negotiated during login, and is keyed from the login itself, so no certificate is involved.</p>

<blockquote>
<img src="../../images/secure-wire-firebird-unsecured.png"/>
</blockquote>
<p>The <i>wirecrypt</i> attribute on the listener tag sets the level of encryption that SQL Relay asks for:</p>

<ul>
  <li><b>disabled</b> - never encrypt.</li>
  <li><b>enabled</b> - encrypt if the client is willing to.  The default.</li>
  <li><b>required</b> - refuse any client that won't encrypt.</li>
</ul>

<p>The client offers its encryption level, and the two are negotiated as follows:</p>

<ul>
  <li>If both sides require or enable encryption, the session is encrypted.</li>
  <li>If both sides disable encryption, the session is not encrypted.</li>
  <li>If one side enables encryption and the other disables it, the session is not encrypted.</li>
  <li>If one side requires encryption and the other disables it, the login is refused.</li>
</ul>

<blockquote>
<!-- Generator: GNU source-highlight 3.1.9
by Lorenzo Bettini
http://www.lorenzobettini.it
http://www.gnu.org/software/src-highlite -->
<pre><tt><b><font color="#000080">&lt;?xml</font></b> <font color="#009900">version</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"1.0"</font><b><font color="#000080">?&gt;</font></b>
<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;instances&gt;</font></b>
	<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;instance</font></b> <font color="#009900">id</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"example"</font> <font color="#009900">dbase</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"firebird"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;listeners&gt;</font></b>
			<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;listener</font></b> <font color="#009900">protocol</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"firebird"</font> <font color="#009900">port</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"3050"</font> <font color="#009900">wirecrypt</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"required"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">/&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/listeners&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;connections&gt;</font></b>
			<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;connection</font></b> <font color="#009900">string</font><font color="#990000">=</font><font color="#FF0000">"user=firebirduser;password=firebirdpassword;db=firebirdhost:/opt/firebird/firebirddb.gdb"</font><b><font color="#0000FF">/&gt;</font></b>
		<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/connections&gt;</font></b>
	<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/instance&gt;</font></b>
<b><font color="#0000FF">&lt;/instances&gt;</font></b>
</tt></pre>

</blockquote>
<p>Note that:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Wire Encryption requires protocol version 13 or higher - see <a href="firebirdprotoversion.html">Protocol Version</a>.</li>
  <li>Only the Arc4 cipher is currently supported.  ChaCha and ChaCha64 are not.</li>
</ul>

<p>See the <a href="../configreference.html#attributes">SQL Relay Configuration Reference</a> for the full description of the <i>wirecrypt</i> option.</p>

